> 
> The most effective is reading a blessed scroll of remove curse, it
> will uncurse your complete visible inventory, but not the objects in
> cotainers (these scrolls cost around 80 Zorkmids in shops). Reading
> an uncursed scroll will just remove curses from worn items (and a few
> specific burdens). You may also cast the spell of the same name.
> Dipping in holy water will uncurse a single cursed item (or a stack
> of items), but that is quite ineffective and should only be used if
> you're in need to do so. Dipping in a fountain may occasionally remove
> the curse ("The water glows for a moment."), but be aware that there
> are bad effects that might happen instead. Specific items that became
> cursed, like a luckstone, a lizard corpse, etc., are better simply
> dropped and replaced by a spare one. Keep backups of items that should
> not become cursed in some bag.

Forgot one important...

Zapping a wand of cancellation will also remove the curses from items.
But depending on the object type other mostly bad side effects happen:
potions may turn to water, scroll and spellbooks turn blank, wands are
emptied, enchantments (positive and negative) will be set to zero, etc.

